}=\psi_0-\mu_\tau$.
For a fixed fold, the true Doob--Meyer decomposition gives
\begin{align}
\label{eq:fitted-score-decomposition}
\widehat\psi_{-k}-\psi_0
&=
\mu_{\widehat A^{(-k)}}(\tau\mid X)-\mu_{A_0}(\tau\mid X) \\
&\quad+
\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal J}\int_0^\tau
\{\widehat H_{\ell}^{(-k)}-H_{\ell,0}\}(u,X)\,dM_{\ell,0}(u) \notag \\
&\quad-
\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal J}\int_0^\tau
Y_{j(\ell)}(u)\widehat H_{\ell}^{(-k)}(u,X)\,dD_{k,\ell}(u\mid X). \notag
\end{align}
The first term is bounded by
$|\mu_{\widehat A^{(-k)}}(\tau\mid x)-\mu_{A_0}(\tau\mid x)| \le 2\tau\kappa_{-k}(x) \le C\delta_{A,-k}(x).$
For the second, positivity and the residual-RMST representation give
\[
\max_{\ell\in\mathcal J}\sup_{u\le\tau}
|\widehat H_{\ell}^{(-k)}(u,x)-H_{\ell,0}(u,x)|
\le C\{\kappa_{-k}(x)+\eta_{-k}(x)\}.
\]
The martingale isometry, finiteness of the transition set, and bounded
true hazard mass imply
$\left\| \sum_{\ell\in\mathcal J}\int_0^\tau (\widehat H_{\ell}^{(-k)}-H_{\ell,0})dM_{\ell,0} \right\|_{L_2(P)} =O_p(a_N+c_N).$
For the last term of \eqref{eq:fitted-score-decomposition}, apply
\[
\left|\int_{(0,\tau]}f(u)dD(u)\right|
\le
2\|D\|_{\infty,\tau}
\left\{\|f\|_{\infty,\tau}+\operatorname{pvar}(f;[0,\tau])\right\},
\]
which holds for finite-variation $f,D$ with $D(0)=0$.
Lemma~\ref{lem:rmst-weight-variation}, applied to the fitted transition and
censoring laws, gives uniformly on $\mathcal E_N$
\[
\sup_u|Y_{j(\ell)}(u)\widehat H_{\ell}^{(-k)}(u,X)|
+
\operatorname{pvar}\{Y_{j(\ell)}\widehat H_{\ell}^{(-k)};[0,\tau]\}
\le C_{\tau,g_0,M}.
\]
Hence
$\left| \sum_{\ell\in\mathcal J}\int_0^\tau Y_{j(\ell)}\widehat H_{\ell}^{(-k)}dD_{k,\ell} \right| \le C\delta_{A,-k}(X),$
with $L_2(P)$-norm $O_p(a_N)$. Combining these bounds in
\eqref{eq:fitted-score-decomposition} yields
$\max_{1\le k\le K} \|\widehat\psi_{-k}-\psi_0\|_{L_2(P)} =O_p(a_N+c_N).$
Thus fitted-score stability follows from the stated nuisance conditions.

