Conditional on $\mathcal D_{-k}$, the variance of the middle fold term is at most
$m_k^{-1}\|\widehat\psi_{-k}-\psi_0\|_{L_2(P)}^2.$
Since $K$ is fixed and $m_k\asymp N$,
$\sum_{k=1}^K\frac{m_k}{N} (\mathbb P_{I_k}-P)(\widehat\psi_{-k}-\psi_0) =O_p\{N^{-1/2}(a_N+c_N)\}.$
The bias bound \eqref{eq:fold-bias-product-rate} gives
$\left|\sum_{k=1}^K\frac{m_k}{N}B_{k,N}\right| \le \max_k|B_{k,N}|=O_p(a_Nc_N).$
Substitution into \eqref{eq:crossfit-canonical-decomposition} proves
\eqref{eq:main-os-canonical-expansion}. Since $a_N+c_N=o(1)$,
\eqref{eq:main-os-canonical-rate} also follows. Under $a_Nc_N=o(N^{-1/2})$, both
remainders are $o_p(N^{-1/2})$, establishing the canonical asymptotic linear
expansion.
